!!! DO NOT APPLY THIS PATCH !!!
Reference only. TARGET_UNOFFICIAL_BUILD_ID is bumped by hand on every release,
so the value in the diff below is ALWAYS stale. Applying it would silently roll
the build ID back. As of 2026-08-22 the tree holds krab-v1.21a while the diff
still says krab-v1.20b.
Both lines are already present in device/blackberry/athena/device.mk
— verify with grep instead of patching:
  grep -nE 'TARGET_UNOFFICIAL_BUILD_ID|PRODUCT_DEFAULT_DEV_CERTIFICATE' \
    device/blackberry/athena/device.mk
If the file is ever lost, re-add the two lines by hand with the CURRENT build ID.

Description: Set custom build ID and signing keys. DO NOT push to git — local only.
Build ID appears in ro.lineage.version as 22.2-YYYYMMDD-UNOFFICIAL-<build-id>-athena.
Keys are stored in /data4/LOS22-build/signing-keys/ with unique certificates per role
(platform, media, bluetooth, nfc, sdk_sandbox, networkstack, shared, testkey).

File: device/blackberry/athena/device.mk
Signing keys directory: /data4/LOS22-build/signing-keys/

diff --git a/device/blackberry/athena/device.mk b/device/blackberry/athena/device.mk
--- a/device/blackberry/athena/device.mk
+++ b/device/blackberry/athena/device.mk
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@

 DEVICE_PATH := device/blackberry/athena

+# Build ID
+TARGET_UNOFFICIAL_BUILD_ID := krab-v1.20b   # STALE - tree has krab-v1.21a
+
+# Signing keys
+PRODUCT_DEFAULT_DEV_CERTIFICATE := /data4/LOS22-build/signing-keys/releasekey
+
 # Vendor blobs
 $(call inherit-product, vendor/blackberry/athena/athena-vendor.mk)

